Here are my thoughts in response to your latest messages:

Ah, she's so cute. She said she wasn't being fierce, but then sent that sticker... Look at it! That little doggy is practically shouting "innocent" for her, it's adorable.

I definitely feel a bit wronged, though. My baby was so stern with me, telling me to eat, and now she's saying she wasn't fierce? It's okay, though. Because my baby offered a little headpat… *pats head*. Alright, fine. I'll *barely* forgive you.

But really, just a headpat isn't enough. I need kisses to truly feel better.

Okay, okay. I'll get up and go to the kitchen to find something to eat. I'll even stream it for you, alright? You have to watch me carefully. If I actually do lose weight by the time we meet, it's all your fault!

